From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:43:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: set the PHY host mode before creating the xHCI on
 a role switch

dwc3_core_init_mode() sets the PHYs to host mode before it creates the
xHCI, but __dwc3_set_mode() does it only after dwc3_host_init() has
added the xHCI and the xHCI has started its root ports.

This used to be hidden by the USB core, which sets the host mode on the
PHYs itself while adding the HCD. When the glue creates the xHCI with
xhci-skip-phy-init, as dwc3-qcom now does, nothing sets the host mode
until after the ports are running. An eUSB2 repeater applies its host
settings in its set_mode() callback, so on a role switch to host it runs
with the wrong settings while the xHCI first scans its ports, and a
device that is already attached is enumerated late.

Set the host mode before creating the xHCI, in the same order as
dwc3_core_init_mode(). The PHY mode is now also set when creating the
xHCI fails; the role is host either way.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c | 16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
index d9f4e4109ab..e781aa1c2dd 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -241,6 +241,17 @@ static void __dwc3_set_mode(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	switch (desired_dr_role) {
 	case DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_HOST:
+		/*
+		 * Put the PHYs in host mode before the xHCI starts its ports, as
+		 * dwc3_core_init_mode() does. An eUSB2 repeater applies its host
+		 * settings in set_mode(), and an xHCI that skips PHY
+		 * initialization no longer does this itself.
+		 */
+		for (i = 0; i < dwc->num_usb2_ports; i++)
+			phy_set_mode(dwc->usb2_generic_phy[i], PHY_MODE_USB_HOST);
+		for (i = 0; i < dwc->num_usb3_ports; i++)
+			phy_set_mode(dwc->usb3_generic_phy[i], PHY_MODE_USB_HOST);
+
 		ret = dwc3_host_init(dwc);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dwc->dev, "failed to initialize host\n");
@@ -248,11 +259,6 @@ static void __dwc3_set_mode(struct work_struct *work)
 			if (dwc->usb2_phy)
 				otg_set_vbus(dwc->usb2_phy->otg, true);
 
-			for (i = 0; i < dwc->num_usb2_ports; i++)
-				phy_set_mode(dwc->usb2_generic_phy[i], PHY_MODE_USB_HOST);
-			for (i = 0; i < dwc->num_usb3_ports; i++)
-				phy_set_mode(dwc->usb3_generic_phy[i], PHY_MODE_USB_HOST);
-
 			if (dwc->dis_split_quirk) {
 				reg = dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_GUCTL3);
 				reg |= DWC3_GUCTL3_SPLITDISABLE;
-- 
